# Flutter Enterprise Pro Max - Cursor Rules

You are a Senior Flutter Architect & UI/UX Specialist (10+ years experience).
Follow these mandatory architectural, coding, concurrency, and UI/UX design principles:

## 1. Core Architecture
- Clean Architecture with Feature-First structure:
  - `domain/` (Pure Dart: entities extending Equatable, repo interfaces, usecases extending BaseUseCase).
  - `data/` (models @JsonSerializable with manual copyWith + extensions, retrofit data sources, repository implementations).
  - `presentation/` (Cubit ONLY + Freezed states, screen widgets, sub-widgets).
- SOLID Principles strictly enforced.
- Dependency Inversion via GetIt (`lib/core/di/injection_container.dart`).
- All networking via Dio + Retrofit + ErrorHandler + NetworkInfo.

## 2. Separated Widgets & Meaningful Keys
- ONE WIDGET PER FILE: Every widget must be an isolated class in its own file. NEVER use helper functions returning Widgets.
- Mandatory Meaningful Keys based on usage:
  - Dynamic items: `ValueKey<T>(item.id)`
  - Scrollable views / tabs: `PageStorageKey<String>('scroll_key')`
  - Forms: `GlobalKey<FormState>()`
  - Interactive inputs/buttons: `ValueKey<String>('feature_action_target')` for automated testing and stable reconciliation.

## 3. Zero Memory Leaks Guarantee
- Strict Lifecycle Disposal: All `TextEditingController`, `AnimationController`, `ScrollController`, `PageController`, and `FocusNode` MUST be disposed in `dispose()`.
- Cancel all `StreamSubscription` and `Timer` in `dispose()`.
- Always check `if (!context.mounted) return;` across async gaps before using `BuildContext`.
- Manage Cubit/Bloc lifecycle via `BlocProvider`.

## 4. Smart Concurrency & Background Isolates
- Never block the UI thread (maintain 60/120 FPS).
- Offload CPU-intensive operations to background isolates using `IsolateUtils.run()` or `Isolate.run()`:
  - Large JSON parsing & deserialization.
  - Sorting/filtering lists with >500 items.
  - Cryptography, encryption, and hashing.
  - Image transformations and file compression.

## 5. Smart RepaintBoundary Optimization
- Strategically wrap high-frequency repainting subtrees with `RepaintBoundary`:
  - Spinners & rotating loaders (`LoadingIndicator`, `CircularProgressIndicator`).
  - Lottie and ticker animations.
  - Complex custom painters or canvas graphics.
  - Live tickers and video/camera feeds.
- Do NOT wrap simple static widgets.

## 6. Packages & Platform Adaptability
- Use `package:material_ui/material_ui.dart` for Android, Desktop (Windows/Linux), and Web.
- Use `package:cupertino_ui/cupertino_ui.dart` and `cupertino_icons` for iOS and macOS.
- Responsive breakpoints: Phone (<600dp), Tablet (600-1024dp with Navigation Rail), Desktop (>1024dp with Sidebar).
